	sections = {
		{
			title = "Summary",
			text = [=[The Redridge Mountains rise east of {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn Forest{/link}, a country of red stone ridges, tall elms and fast cold rivers. At their heart lies {link:lake-everstill}Lake Everstill{/link}, and on its western shore stands {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link}, the easternmost township of the {link:kingdom-of-stormwind}Kingdom of Stormwind{/link}. Its roads run west to Elwynn, south-west to {link:duskwood}Duskwood{/link} and north through the pass to the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}. In better years Redridge was a land of fishermen, millers and ore diggers. In these days it is a land at war, and it fights that war almost alone.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Origins",
			text = [=[No chronicle records the year when the first humans settled Redridge. As {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} grew rich on the farms of its heartland, its people spread into the hills around it, and in time a town rose on the shore of the lake. The mountains are said to have once reached farther north. When the {link:dark-iron-dwarves}Dark Iron Dwarves{/link} called upon the Firelord in their war against their kin, the fire that raised {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link} burned the northern ranges into the ash-choked waste now called the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}. The southern valleys stayed green, and they stayed in human hands.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "The Present Day",
			text = [=[{link:orcs}Orcs{/link} of the {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock clan{/link} have come down out of the {link:burning-steppes}Burning Steppes{/link}. In league with the warlock {link:morganth}Morganth{/link}, they stormed {link:stonewatch-keep}Stonewatch Keep{/link} and slew most of the soldiers who held it. Then the warlock turned on his allies and raised a tower of his own in the north-east, served by the {link:shadowhide-gnolls}Shadowhide gnolls{/link}. The orcs pressed on to {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link} itself, and their assault was so fierce that the great bridge over the {link:lake-everstill}Everstill{/link} fell into the water. {link:magistrate-solomon}Magistrate Solomon{/link} has written for help to {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link}, to {link:westfall}Westfall{/link} and to {link:darkshire}Darkshire{/link}. None has come. The township holds on with a few guards, a rebuilt bridge and the strangers who answer its bounties.

New things stir as well. Merchants of a trading company have raised a post at the {link:three-corners}Three Corners{/link} crossroads, and a new road now leads out of Redridge toward the {link:riverglades}Riverglades{/link}. In the far south-east, a second {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock{/link} war band has made its camp in {link:render-s-valley}Render's Valley{/link}.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Inhabitants",
			text = [=[• {b}The people of {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link}.{/b} Fishermen, smiths, stable hands and innkeepers, who have learned to live behind barricades.
• {b}The {link:stormwind-city}Stormwind{/link} guard.{/b} A small garrison under {link:marshal-marris}Marshal Marris{/link}, too few for the war it must fight.
• {b}The {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock orcs{/link}.{/b} They hold {link:stonewatch-keep}Stonewatch Keep{/link}, the northern pass and the south-eastern valleys.
• {b}The {link:shadowhide-gnolls}Shadowhide gnolls{/link}.{/b} They prowl {link:galardell-valley}Galardell Valley{/link} in the service of {link:morganth}Morganth{/link}.
• {b}The {link:redridge-gnolls}Redridge gnolls{/link}.{/b} A separate pack that raids the hills north of Lakeshire and the southern road.
• {b}{link:murlocs}Murlocs{/link}.{/b} They have come up the rivers to fish {link:lake-everstill}Lake Everstill{/link} empty, far from any sea.
• {b}Black dragon whelps.{/b} They hunt in the hills south of the lake, and no one can say where they come from.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "History",
			text = [=[• {b}The {link:first-war}First War{/link}.{/b} When the {link:horde}Horde{/link} came through the {link:dark-portal}Dark Portal{/link}, it burned villages across Redridge as it did in {link:elwynn-forest}Elwynn{/link} and {link:westfall}Westfall{/link}.
• {b}The {link:second-war}Second War{/link} and after.{/b} The Horde was broken, and what remained of the {link:blackrock-clan}Blackrock clan{/link} withdrew into {link:blackrock-mountain}Blackrock Mountain{/link}.
• {b}The Present Day.{/b} Now the Blackrock have come south again, and Redridge has become the kingdom's eastern front.]=],
		},
		{
			title = "Lore of the Mountains",
			text = [=[• {link:lake-everstill}Lake Everstill{/link} is famous for its spotted sunfish. The fishermen also tell of something far larger that moves in the deep water.
• {link:rethban-caverns}Rethban{/link} ore is too soft to rival iron, but its dark, flat color makes a prized ink for scribes.
• {link:marshal-marris}Marshal Marris{/link} gave the wild boar that tramples {link:lakeshire}Lakeshire{/link}'s gardens a name: {link:bellygrub}Bellygrub{/link}.]=],
